---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Search across your curriculum — apprenti.dev Docs">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold">
                Search across your curriculum
            </h1>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">
            <section>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    <strong>Search</strong> looks across everything the app
                    has projected from your repository — fully offline,
                    with no query ever leaving the device.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    What's indexed
                </h2>
                <ul class="space-y-1 text-muted-foreground mt-2">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Curriculum,
                        terms, modules, tasks
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Task titles and
                        full instructions
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Your
                        reflections
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Mentor notes
                        and feedback you've synced
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Resource titles
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                        <span class="text-link mt-1">•</span>Competency
                        descriptions
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    Type a task title, a task id, or just a word from the
                    instructions — the hint text says exactly that: <em
                        >"Task title, id, or a word from the
                        instructions."</em
                    >
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">Filters</h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Narrow results by type, year, term, module, status,
                    competency, or resource provider when a search returns
                    more than you want to scan.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">
                    Why it's instant
                </h2>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                    Search runs against the on-device projection (SQLite
                    full-text search), not against Git or the network. That
                    projection can always be rebuilt from your repository,
                    so a search index that gets out of sync is a
                    non-issue — it's a cache, not a second source of truth.
                    If you work across more than one curriculum, search
                    stays scoped to whichever one is currently active, so
                    results from a different apprenticeship never bleed
                    in.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 flex gap-4">
            <a href="/docs" class="text-sm text-link hover:underline"
                >← All Docs</a
            >
            <a href="/" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:underline"
                >Back to apprenti.dev</a
            >
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
